      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T13:28:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Whether to wrap it in a module should be configurable.\n\nFor library variants this adds an additional level of hierarchy that seems unnecessary, e.g.\n\n   my_proto_crate_name::my_proto_mod_wrapper::\n\nMy thoughts are we shouldn\u0027t pass this flag when generating the code for library variants, but then it also means that our library variants are generating different source which doesn\u0027t seem great either.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8ffa160_3d6deab0",
        "filename": "rust/protobuf.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
