        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-28T21:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have been back-and-forth on this choice.\nI think the trouble of additional layer can be reduced into one extra \"use declaration\" in user code to introduce a short alias. As you said, applying wrap_in_module\u003d\u003csource_stem\u003e gives consistent module name to the generated code, no matter it is included, imported, or linked.\n\nAnother design choice is to make \"source_stem\" optional and not to wrap-in-module without source_stem. Or we can make that choice later when there are more use cases.",
      "parentUuid": "ce976df9_fbf9c058",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "2e58dfae5f8e6156e0a225023d2abe860f555e25",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
